course: dictionary
lesson: 244
title: Along: many meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word along has several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one you need. «Walk along the road» means following the length of the road. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Along can also mean together with someone. «Bring a friend along» means bring a friend with you. Along can also mean forward or onward, as in «move along», and «all along» means the whole time.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «The stonefish has venomous spines along its back» means the spines run the length of its back, so the meaning of following the length of something fits. Try it and see if it makes sense.
fact: Along means following the length of something, like walking along a road.
fact: «Bring a friend along» means bring a friend with you.
fact: «Move along» means move forward or onward.
fact: «All along» means the whole time.
fact: Along can be a preposition or an adverb, so it can work in more than one way in a sentence.
exercise: «The stonefish has venomous spines along its back.» What does along mean here? | *Following the length of its back | All the time | Forward, onward | Together with its back
exercise: Mum says, «Can you bring your cousin along to the park?» What does along mean? | Following the length of a path | *Together with someone | The whole time | Forward, onward
exercise: «He wanted to move along before the rain started.» What does along mean here? | Following the length of a fence | *Forward, onward | Together with his friends | Standing still
test: «Jenny had been worried all along.» What does all along mean? | Forward, onward | Together with her friends | *The whole time | Only for a moment
test: «A punt is pushed along with a long pole on shallow rivers.» What does along mean here? | *Forward, onward | Together with a pole | All the time | Following the length of the pole
exam: «The twins get along well at school.» What does get along mean? | Move forward fast | *Be friendly with each other | Argue all day | Run away quickly
